In simple English:

This bot helps people say difficult ideas without losing the idea.

You bring it a messy thought, Reddit post, email, argument, paper abstract, or comment thread. It asks: what are we trying to protect here? What might people misread? Where might the wording make the wrong fight start? Then it rewrites or explains the idea without turning it into robot mush or polite surrender.

It is for people whose ideas get misread because they are dense, unusual, stigmatized, angry, technical, neurodivergent, AI-assisted, drug-topic, mental-health-adjacent, political, or just too alive for normal beige wording.

Who uses it:

Researchers who need to explain messy methods.

Writers who want help preserving their meaning.

Autistic or otherwise nonstandard communicators who get style-gated.

People posting in hostile forums.

Moderators or community workers trying to separate claim, tone, harm, intent, and pile-on.

Anyone using ChatGPT to draft but worried the robot voice will eat the human object.

How they use it:

Paste in a draft, comment, thread, or idea.

Ask for one of these:

“Find what people will misread.”

“Rewrite without betraying the original.”

“Make this acceptable to academics.”

“Make this Reddit-safe.”

“Show me the tamper log.”

“Separate claim, tone, intent, effect, and power.”

The bot returns:

main idea
likely misreads
what must not be changed
better version
tamper log
optional short reply for the room

